{{About|{{ll|Build 42}} crafting recipes|crafting recipes for {{ll|Build 41}}|Recipe (scripts)}}
<translate>
<!--T:1-->
The '''craftRecipe''' {{ll|Scripts|script}} block is used to define a crafting recipe, which allows players to craft items or tiles in the game based on the parent script block. For example, a craftRecipe defined inside a
</translate> <translate><!--T:2--> [https://pz-wiki-modding.github.io/PZ-API-Docs/scripts/module.html module]</translate> <translate><!--T:3--> will be a recipe to craft an item usually, while when defined inside an</translate> <translate><!--T:4--> [https://pz-wiki-modding.github.io/PZ-API-Docs/scripts/entity.html entity]</translate> <translate><!--T:5-->
it will be the building recipe for that entity.

<!--T:6-->
A craftRecipe will usually require an {{ll|Inputs (scripts)|inputs}} and {{ll|Outputs (scripts)|outputs}} block. Other parameters are used to define properties of this recipe, such as the</translate> <translate><!--T:7--> [https://pz-wiki-modding.github.io/PZ-API-Docs/scripts/craftrecipe.html#time time]</translate> <translate><!--T:8--> it takes to craft or the</translate> <translate><!--T:9--> [https://pz-wiki-modding.github.io/PZ-API-Docs/scripts/craftrecipe.html#xpaward XP awarded]</translate> <translate>
<!--T:10-->
for crafting it.

<!--T:11-->
For example:
</translate>
{{CodeSnip
| lang = cpp
| code = 
module yourModule /* or Base */
{
    craftRecipe yourRecipeID
    {
        ...
    }
}
}}

<translate>
<!--T:12-->
To define a {{ll|translation}} for this recipe, you need to create an entry in the translation file
</translate> <translate><!--T:13--> [https://pz-wiki-modding.github.io/PZ-API-Docs/translations/translation_files.html#recipes Recipes.json]</translate><translate>
<!--T:14-->
. The translation entry should be formatted like this:
</translate>
{{CodeSnip
| lang = json
| code = 
{
  "yourRecipeID": "Your recipe"
}
}}

<translate>
<!--T:15-->
Notice how you shouldn't use the
</translate> <translate><!--T:16--> [https://pz-wiki-modding.github.io/PZ-API-Docs/scripts/module.html module]</translate> <translate>
<!--T:17-->
in the translation file key and only the craftRecipe ID.

== craftingRecipe format == <!--T:18-->

<!--T:19-->
To create a new crafting recipe, simply use the following entry in a script file:
</translate>
{{CodeSnip
| lang = java
| code =
module yourModule /* or Base */
{
    craftRecipe <RecipeID>
    {
        ...
    }
}
}}

<translate>
<!--T:20-->
The <code><RecipeID></code> is a unique identifier for the recipe, and '''should not have spaces in it'''. It is used to define the name of the recipe in the {{ll|Translations|translation files}}, in <code>Recipes.json</code>. For example, if the <code><RecipeID></code> is <code>MyRecipe</code>, the translation file for English needs to have:
</translate>
{{CodeSnip
| lang = json
| code =
{
    "MyRecipe": "My recipe name"
}
}}

<translate>
== craftRecipe parameters == <!--T:21-->

<!--T:22-->
You can find a full list of the parameters in the
</translate> <translate><!--T:23--> [https://pz-wiki-modding.github.io/PZ-API-Docs/scripts/craftrecipe.html ScriptsDocs]</translate><translate><!--T:24-->
.

<!--T:25-->
You can also learn more about specific elements of the craftRecipe script block in the following pages:
* {{ll|Fluids (craftRecipe)|Fluids}}
* {{ll|Inputs (scripts)|inputs}}
* {{ll|Outputs (scripts)|outputs}}
* {{ll|ItemMapper (scripts)|itemMapper}}

=== Available skills === <!--T:26-->

<!--T:27-->
You can define multiple skills and their respective experience points/levels by separating them with <code>;</code>. Below is how each parameters need to be formatted:
* {{ll|xpAward}} format is <code>skill:experience</code>
* {{ll|SkillRequired}} format is <code>skill:level</code>
* {{ll|AutoLearnAll}} format is <code>skill:level</code>
* {{ll|AutoLearnAny}} format is <code>skill:level</code>

<!--T:28-->
You can find the available skills in the</translate> {{JavaObject|package=zombie/characters/skills|PerkFactory.Perks}} <translate>
<!--T:29-->
class. Alternatively, you can also use modded skills defined by your mod or other mods.

